%% Composite figures (PART 9 S4c). A BARE `::: figure` opener is one figure of
%% ordered panels; the same opener carrying a title or a [label] is not.

::: figure

![One](one.png)
^ Panel one.

![Two](two.png)
^ Panel two.

:::
^ The group caption, an ordinary caption line below the closing fence.

%% A title makes it a generic container, not a group.

::: figure "Titled"
Generic container.
:::

%% A label does too.

::: figure [g]
Generic container.
:::

%% And both together.

::: figure "Titled" [g]
Generic container.
:::

%% The separator is a space run, never a tab: the line below is a paragraph in
%% Carve, so the group scope must not claim it.

:::	figure

%% A longer fence opens a group just as three colons do.

:::: figure
Panels.
::::

%% A group may open directly after a list marker.

- ::: figure

%% Neither `figures` nor a trailing word is the reserved kind word.

::: figures
Generic container.
:::

